            <ArticleTitle>Calcium channel blocking drugs for chronic, stable angina. Verapamil.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>19-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Verapamil is effective primary therapy for angina pectoris at a dosage of about 120 mg three times a day. In equal doses it has the same antianginal effect as propranolol although the mechanism of action is different. Long-term therapy is effective and well tolerated. Side effects are few and if required, verapamil may be given with nitrates or beta-blockers.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
